  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ensuring Safe Migration by Institutionalizing a Migration Support Centre in Bangalore, India</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Migration for survival and migration for sustenance, which pushed a large segment of the population to move towards urban areas, have failed to ensure better livelihood opportunities and a better future for migrants. Migrant workers encounter challenges such as a lack of suitable accommodation, sub-standard living conditions, low wages, and inaccessibility to social security schemes and services due to lack of required identity cards and other necessary documents. With the aforementioned challenges in mind, IOM India will partner with Shahi Exports, one of India&#x2019;s largest apparel manufacturers, to strengthen functioning modalities of the Shahi Exports supported Migrant Support Centre (MSC) in Bangalore, India.  It is envisaged that the partnership will help catering to the needs of the migrant workers and facilitate support for accommodation, counselling services, identity documentation services, linking with healthcare services, networking with employers, grievance redressal, and other key services relevant for migrants.</narrative>
  </description>
